{
  "$schema": "./_schema/entity.v1.schema.json",
  "entity": {
    "id": "V09",
    "title": "Self-contained Tokens"
  },
  "rule_set": {
    "version": "0.1.17",
    "timestamp": "2026-11-09T11:37:40Z",
    "hash": "blake3:49678333f6ad32635a429ad5b43708d6b7fe70970bb08a3bd6755b2144cdaf6c"
  },
  "rules": [],
  "sub_entities": [
    {
      "$schema": "./_schema/entity.v1.schema.json",
      "entity": {
        "id": "V09S01",
        "title": "Token source and integrity",
        "parent": "V09"
      },
      "rule_set": {
        "version": "0.1.6",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-09T11:37:40Z",
        "hash": "blake3:cdaeef1b5ef03c03bf76978ecc0cd88f1a6409865660dfeebe332dd571a7db60"
      },
      "rules": [
        {
          "id": "V09S01-001",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "Verify that self-contained tokens are validated using their digital signature or MAC to protect against tampering before accepting the token's contents.",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.1.1",
          "profiles": [
            "L1",
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "V09S01-002",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "Verify that only algorithms on an allowlist can be used to create and verify self-contained tokens, for a given context.",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.1.2",
          "profiles": [
            "L1",
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "V09S01-003",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "The allowlist must include the permitted algorithms, ideally only either symmetric or asymmetric algorithms, and must not include the 'None' algorithm.",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.1.2",
          "profiles": [
            "L1",
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "V09S01-004",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "If both symmetric and asymmetric must be supported, additional controls will be needed to prevent key confusion.",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.1.2",
          "profiles": [
            "L1",
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "V09S01-005",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "Verify that key material that is used to validate self-contained tokens is from trusted pre-configured sources for the token issuer, preventing attackers from specifying untrusted sources and keys.",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.1.3",
          "profiles": [
            "L1",
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "V09S01-006",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "For JWTs and other JWS structures, headers such as 'jku', 'x5u', and 'jwk' must be validated against an allowlist of trusted sources.",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.1.3",
          "profiles": [
            "L1",
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "$schema": "./_schema/entity.v1.schema.json",
      "entity": {
        "id": "V09S02",
        "title": "Token content",
        "parent": "V09"
      },
      "rule_set": {
        "version": "0.1.9",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-09T11:37:40Z",
        "hash": "blake3:20eb4f170c71c2f294a69a44d8a52c0cd6eeedc06d5d3a26afa0de197afefa13"
      },
      "rules": [
        {
          "id": "V09S02-001",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "Verify that, if a validity time span is present in the token data, the token and its content are accepted only if the verification time is within this validity time span.",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.2.1",
          "profiles": [
            "L1",
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "V09S02-002",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "For example, for JWTs, the claims 'nbf' and 'exp' must be verified.",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.2.1",
          "profiles": [
            "L1",
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "V09S02-003",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "Verify that the service receiving a token validates the token to be the correct type and is meant for the intended purpose before accepting the token's contents.",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.2.2",
          "profiles": [
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "V09S02-004",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "For example, only access tokens can be accepted for authorization decisions and only ID Tokens can be used for proving user authentication.",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.2.2",
          "profiles": [
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "V09S02-005",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "Verify that the service only accepts tokens which are intended for use with that service (audience).",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.2.3",
          "profiles": [
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "V09S02-006",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "For JWTs, this can be achieved by validating the 'aud' claim against an allowlist defined in the service.",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.2.3",
          "profiles": [
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "V09S02-007",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "Verify that, if a token issuer uses the same private key for issuing tokens to different audiences, the issued tokens contain an audience restriction that uniquely identifies the intended audiences.",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.2.4",
          "profiles": [
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "V09S02-008",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "This will prevent a token from being reused with an unintended audience.",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.2.4",
          "profiles": [
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "V09S02-009",
          "revision": 0,
          "state": "D",
          "body": "If the audience identifier is dynamically provisioned, the token issuer must validate these audiences in order to make sure that they do not result in audience impersonation.",
          "added_by": "github:pleberre",
          "added_at": "2026-11-09",
          "supersedes": null,
          "clause": "V9.2.4",
          "profiles": [
            "L2",
            "L3"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "notes": []
    }
  ],
  "notes": []
}
